t":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":701.4452629101562,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.64,"r":286.07328,"t":725.4707029101563},"charspan":[0,77],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"The minimum I-CVI and  the  computed S-CVI for the study module were 0.78 and"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"0.93,respectively (Table 2). The minimum value of I-CVI was given to items 5, 10 and 11 (0.78) and Items 1-4 and 12-16 had the complete value (1.00) (Table 2).","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":701.4452629101562,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.81,"r":541.3112799999998,"t":754.5107029101563},"charspan":[0,159],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"0.93,respectively (Table 2). The minimum value of I-CVI was given to items 5, 10 and 11 (0.78) and Items 1-4 and 12-16 had the complete value (1.00) (Table 2)."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Table 2. The ranking of the questionnaire's items according to the experts (n=9)","parent":{"$ref":"#/tables/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":681.8267029101563,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.7,"r":461.08,"t":690.4022629101563},"charspan":[0,80],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"Table 2. The ranking of the questionnaire's items according to the experts (n=9)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Therefore, the results of the assessments showed that the majority of the  experts  believed that the module was valid according to the study population and objectives. However, the essential changes were applied based on the experts' recommendation such as improving the activities details and steps, adding picture to the module as well as highlighting the target life skill(s) in each session.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":256.76526291015625,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.64,"r":286.19911999999994,"t":382.7007029101563},"charspan":[0,396],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"Therefore, the results of the assessments showed that the majority of the  experts  believed that the module was valid according to the study population and objectives. However, the essential changes were applied based on the experts' recommendation such as improving the activities details and steps, adding picture to the module as well as highlighting the target life skill(s) in each session."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Face Validity","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":236.04808472833815,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":68.064,"r":131.9304,"t":245.33406291015626},"charspan":[0,13],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"Face Validity"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Most  of  the  participants  in  both  groups  were female  (19  females  vs.  11  males)  with  Malay ethnicity (14 Malay vs. 7 Chinese and 9 Indian). Although  the  participants  did  not  live  with  their parents,  40.2%  of  them  had  at  least  one  living parent.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":148.88526291015637,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.64,"r":286.18760000000003,"t":231.1107029101563},"charspan":[0,271],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"Most  of  the  participants  in  both  groups  were female  (19  females  vs.  11  males)  with  Malay ethnicity (14 Malay vs. 7 Chinese and 9 Indian). Although  the  participants  did  not  live  with  their parents,  40.2%  of  them  had  at  least  one  living parent."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Using Paired Samples t-Test, the results showed that the mean score of 6 coping methods including active coping (t=-5.85, P<0.001), using of emotional supports(t=-4.80, P<0.001), using of instrumental  support  (t=-4.89,  P<0.001),  positive reframing(t=-3.89, P<0.001), planning(t=-4.91, P<0.001) and acceptance (t=-5.98, P<0.001) methods significantly increased after interventional sessions. Meanwhile, the mean score of 3 coping methods including selfdistraction  (t=5.43,  P<0.001),  denial  (t  =  2.80, P<0.02) and self-blame (t=7.24, P < 0.001) significantly decreased in post-test. No significant change was found in mean score of substance use, behavior disengagement, venting, humor and religion (p>0.05).","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":154.88526291015637,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":311.81,"r":541.42,"t":382.7007029101563},"charspan":[0,716],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"Using Paired Samples t-Test, the results showed that the mean score of 6 coping methods including active coping (t=-5.85, P<0.001), using of emotional supports(t=-4.80, P<0.001), using of instrumental  support  (t=-4.89,  P<0.001),  positive reframing(t=-3.89, P<0.001), planning(t=-4.91, P<0.001) and acceptance (t=-5.98, P<0.001) methods significantly increased after interventional sessions. Meanwhile, the mean score of 3 coping methods including selfdistraction  (t=5.43,  P<0.001),  denial  (t  =  2.80, P<0.02) and self-blame (t=7.24, P < 0.001) significantly decreased in post-test. No significant change was found in mean score of substance use, behavior disengagement, venting, humor and religion (p>0.05)."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"226","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":43.125335637428975,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":56.64,"r":74.154,"t":51.50290291015631},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/11","text":"226"}],"version":"1.10.0"}